WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.969
NARRATOR: Researchers
have confirmed

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.738
100 bull shark attacks.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:13.580
But the real number may be much
higher because the bull shark

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.348
is so difficult to identify.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.254
When you first
look at a bull shark,

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:24.124
it doesn't really jump out at
you that it's a bull shark.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.492
It just kind of looks
like other sharks.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.128
You have kind of grayish
brown on top, white below.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.731
That's really different from an
iconic species like the tiger

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.100
shark that has that
really square head

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:38.304
and those stripes that set it
apart from any other species.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.807
And then you also
have white sharks.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.776
Nobody's going to
mistake a white shark.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.211
This is a really iconic look.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:49.883
You have the torpedo shape, the
tail, the bright white belly,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.386
slate gray above.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:58.892
NARRATOR: The bull shark's
looks aren't showy or iconic.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:04.330
But if you know what to look
for, you'll never forget it.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.867
When you really start to
look closer at the bull sharks,

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.803
you see some
features that differ

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:13.106
from typical shark shape.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.809
They almost look like
swimming mounds in time.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:19.846
They're really thick from
those pectoral fins forward,

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.281
huge jaws.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:25.552
And then, they've got the
musculature to back that up.

